      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. I'll improve understandability by: removing unused imports and data provider methods, extracting the expected result into a named variable, adding a comment explaining the Julian rule, and adding assertion failure messages.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused imports and dead data-provider methods, extracts the expected leap-year boolean into a named variable (`expectedLeapYear`) to clarify intent, adds a comment explaining why the simple Julian `% 4` rule applies for years before the 1752 cutover, and includes failure messages in both assertions to aid debugging."
